    "globalConstraints": "- The synced shape is untouched: `client/src/Store.tsx` \u2014 the one `MergeableStore`, its `createSqliteWasmPersister` and its `createWsSynchronizer` \u2014 and `server/` are byte-identical to BASE, and the tags ride the store like every other cell. A task that opens a second store, a second socket or a second persister is a finding.\n- No new dependency: `package.json`, `client/package.json`, `server/package.json` and `bun.lock` are byte-identical to BASE. Every import this plan adds resolves against what is already installed.\n- The design system's tokens and nothing else: a colour is a declared token of `client/src/index.css`, a class is one Tailwind generates, a shadcn component (`Button`, `Input`, `Badge`) is restyled only through its variants \u2014 the six `@shadcn/lint` rules are the definition and `bun run lint:ui`'s word is final. A raw colour, an inline `style=`, an arbitrary value or a class outside the system is a finding.\n- No schema `default` on the `tags` cell or the `tag` value: a todo with no tags has no `tags` cell, a store with no tag filter has no `tag` value, and every seed and expected file checked in before this plan loads through `createTodosStore` to itself byte for byte. A `default` on anything this plan adds is a finding.\n- Every control this plan adds carries an accessible name \u2014 the tags box is named `Tags for <todo text>`, a chip is named `Tag <tag>` \u2014 and every interaction in an exam names its control by role and name; a view selector is an id, a tag, a `data-*` attribute or shadcn's `data-slot`, never a class of the app's own.\n- `#doneCount`'s text stays exactly `<n> of <m> done`: the linter's own exam pins the literal `<span id=\"doneCount\">1 of 2 done</span>`, so the tagged total is its own element `#taggedCount` beside it and never a change to that span.\n- The linter's four test files under `packages/tinyapp-lint/test/` keep their count and list pins loosened only to containment and tree-computed counts, never re-pinned to a new exact literal (both folds of 2026-09-15). The same rule holds for any exam already on the tree that a task loosens: a pin on the number of inputs in a row is loosened to the id of the one it meant, never re-pinned to the new number.",
